financebench_id_09724,What is Coca Cola's FY2021 COGS % margin? Calculate what was asked by utilizing the line items clearly shown in the income statement.,39.7%,COCACOLA_2021_10K,metrics-generated,"To calculate Coca Cola's FY2021 Cost of Goods Sold (COGS) percentage margin, we use the formula:

\[
\text{COGS % Margin} = \left( \frac{\text{Cost of Goods Sold}}{\text{Net Operating Revenues}} \right) \times 100
\]

From the retrieved income statement for FY2021:
- Cost of Goods Sold (COGS) = \$15,357 million
- Net Operating Revenues = \$38,655 million

Now, substituting these values into the formula:

\[
\text{COGS % Margin} = \left( \frac{15,357}{38,655} \right) \times 100 \approx 39.7\%
\]

Thus, Coca Cola's FY2021 COGS percentage margin is approximately **39.7%**. 

(Source: Coca-Cola FY2021 Income Statement from the retrieved document)",,,"[""COCACOLA_2022_10K"", ""COCACOLA_2021_10K"", ""COCACOLA_2017_10K""]","Source: data\pdfs\COCACOLA_2021_10K.pdf

